  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study and Scale-Up Business Case for Solar-Powered Irrigation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will prepare a detailed feasibility study and develop a scale-up business case for installing approximately 50 solar-powered water-pumping stations in Northern Senegal. It will update CAPEX/OPEX estimates, refine revenue models, and produce an investor pitch to inform the creation of a Special Purpose Vehicle (SPV). The initial cohort will target sites managed by Soci&#xe9;t&#xe9; nationale d&apos;Am&#xe9;nagement et d&apos;Exploitation des Terres du Delta du Fleuve S&#xe9;n&#xe9;gal (SAED) under the Renewable and Efficient Energy Fund (REEF).</narrative>
  </description>
